<title>POLAND: BPH sets up firm for eurobond issue.</title>
<headline>BPH sets up firm for eurobond issue.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Bank Przemyslowo- Handlowy SA (BPH) has formed an Amsterdam-based, fully-owned subsidiary BPH Finance N.V to conduct its convertible eurobond issue, BPH said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>BPH said the firm's capital was 40,000 Dutch guilders.</p>
<p>BPH earlier chose CS First Boston Ltd as the $100-million issue's agent.</p>
<p>It gave no other details and BPH officials were not immediately for comment.</p>
<p>In January the bank's shareholders approved an ex-rights issue of 100,000 five-year convertible bonds of par value at $1,000, exchangeable for up to 1,994,000 shares.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
